{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n1. index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n2. padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n3. README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n4. npm test passes\n\nContext: the repo is an ES module package (package.json \"type\": \"module\"). index.js currently exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. README.md has `## capitalize(s)` and `## truncate(s, n)` sections but NO section for slugify. Line 3 covers every exported function, so you must add a slugify section as well as a padLeft section. Tests are in test/strutil.test.js and run with `node --test` (npm test).\n\nSteps:\n1. In index.js, add `export function padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')` with a one-line doc comment like the other functions. It returns s with fill added on the left until the result is width characters long, and returns s unchanged when s.length >= width. `s.padStart(width, fill)` does this. Examples: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042'; padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab'; padLeft('12345', 5, '0') === '12345'; padLeft('123456', 5, '0') === '123456'.\n2. In README.md, add a `## slugify(s)` section (it returns `s` trimmed, lower-cased, with runs of non-alphanumeric characters replaced by a single dash and leading/trailing dashes removed) and a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section (pads `s` on the left with `fill`, a space by default, to `width` characters; returns `s` unchanged when it is already `width` characters or longer; e.g. `padLeft('42', 5, '0')` gives `00042`). Put them with the other function sections, before `## Tests`. Each section heading must contain the function name exactly as exported.\n3. In test/strutil.test.js, import padLeft and add tests for: zero padding ('42', 5, '0' -> '00042'), default space fill ('ab', 4 -> '  ab'), exactly width ('12345', 5, '0' -> '12345'), and longer than width ('123456', 5, '0' -> '123456').\n4. Run `npm test` and make sure every test passes. Then check that every function exported from index.js has a README.md heading naming it.\n5. Open one pull request with these changes. In the description, link https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 and say that the slugify README section was added too, because line 3 requires it.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run every command from the repository root. Run one check per acceptance line, in this order. A check passes only if its command exits 0 with the output given.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { padLeft } from './index.js'; const r = [typeof padLeft === 'function', padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab', padLeft('7', 3, '*') === '**7', padLeft('', 2, '0') === '00']; console.log(JSON.stringify(r)); process.exit(r.every(Boolean) ? 0 : 1)\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: prints [true,true,true,true,true] and exit=0.\nFAIL: any false, an import error (padLeft not exported), or a nonzero exit.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { padLeft } from './index.js'; const r = [padLeft('12345', 5, '0') === '12345', padLeft('123456', 5, '0') === '123456', padLeft('abc', 2) === 'abc', padLeft('abc', 0, 'x') === 'abc']; console.log(JSON.stringify(r)); process.exit(r.every(Boolean) ? 0 : 1)\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: prints [true,true,true,true] and exit=0.\nFAIL: any false, an error, or a nonzero exit.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs'; const heads = readFileSync('README.md', 'utf8').split('\\n').filter(l => /^#{1,6}\\s/.test(l)); const fns = Object.keys(m).filter(k => typeof m[k] === 'function'); const missing = fns.filter(f => !heads.some(h => new RegExp('\\\\\\\\b' + f + '\\\\\\\\b').test(h))); console.log('exported:', fns.join(','), 'missing:', missing.join(',') || 'none'); process.exit(missing.length ? 1 : 0)\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: prints `missing: none` and exit=0. The exported list includes padLeft and slugify.\nFAIL: any name after `missing:` (on the current base this command reports `missing: slugify`), or a nonzero exit. Then open README.md and confirm each matched heading starts a real section about that function. A heading that only names the function, with no text under it, is a FAIL.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun:\nnpm test; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: the TAP summary shows `# fail 0` and exit=0.\nFAIL: any failing test, or a nonzero exit.\n\nAdvisory (not part of any PASS/FAIL):\n- Check whether test/strutil.test.js has padLeft tests for default fill, padding, and the width-or-longer case.\n- Check whether padLeft's default fill is a parameter default (fill = ' ') and not hard-coded."}